__pycache__/
*.pyc
node_modules/
.svelte-kit/
build/
.env
*.log
# .claude/ is ignored by default (personal state), but the SHARED team setup
# — the guardrail hook, checked-in settings, skills, and subagents — is tracked
# so every clone + CI + future session inherits the same rules. Personal,
# machine-specific config stays local via settings.local.json.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/agents/
.claude/settings.local.json
api/seed_*.py
# CIPH-pi20-LB-5 — explicit un-ignore: the production guardrail must be
# tracked + reviewable + testable in fresh clones, even though the seed
# scripts that USE it are intentionally local-only.
!api/seed_guardrail.py
api/fixtures/
pdfs
frontend/test-results
.vite/

# repo-local deploy artifacts (rsync'd to VPS, never committed)
golive/

# design-review scratch (static mockups)
tmp/

# INC-001 deploy-gate reports (scripts/verify-migration-prod.sh) — local
# evidence with machine-specific timestamps, regenerated on demand
.inc001/

# AI-assistant configuration — operator-local, not part of the product.
# The working agreement, the PreToolUse guardrail hook, the skills and the
# review agent all still live here on disk and still run; they are simply not
# something a public repository should publish or a contributor should need.
CLAUDE.md
.claude/
